    "title": "Fox News hosts fawn over Sydney Sweeney as they resurface American Eagle ad - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Melody Rivera ,\n9 hours ago Fox News is still not tired of talking about Sydney Sweeney’s American Eagle jeans ad .\nTwo months ago, the Anyone But You actress starred in an ad for the apparel company where she is pictured wearing a complete denim ensemble as she lies down, saying, “Genes are passed down from parents to offspring, often determining traits like hair color, personality, and even eye color,” concluding, “My jeans are blue.”\nAt first, the campaign caused a swarm of responses, with a few coming from public figures like Piers Morgan, Lizzo, and Donald Trump, who showed love for the actress under the condition that she was a “registered Republican.” The president’s admiration for the Sydney Sweeney ad has since dried up—just like the rest of the country’s interest, except, of course, over at Fox News .\nREAD MORE: Taylor Swift breaks silence on fans experiencing 'actual amnesia' from Eras Tour\nREAD MORE: Jimmy Kimmel's brutal takedown of Donald Trump in upcoming live shows\nOn the Tuesday, Sept. 30 segment of America Reports, Sandra Smith and John Roberts once again brought up the ad when they heard about the recent comments the CEO of American Eagle made about the campaign.\nThe anchors highlighted Jay Schottenstein’s interview with The Wall Street Journal , where he said, “You can’t run from fear. We stand behind what we did.”\nSandra went on to point out that, despite the controversy, the company saw an increase in sales, attracting almost one million new customers since the ad was released.\nThe host also mentioned she is one of the new customers, saying it was her job to buy a pair as a reporter doing her “due diligence.\"\nShe said, “I bought two pairs of the jeans just to be part of it. They’re great jeans. I get a lot of compliments on them.”\nWhile John hadn’t confessed to purchasing a pair, he did agree with his co-host’s support of the ad.\n“I don’t understand this controversy,” he admitted. “She is a talented young actress. She is a beautiful woman. She has good genes—from a number of different standpoints, not just the ones she is wearing.\"\nHe questioned, “Why people are losing their minds over it is a mystery to me.”\nCritics claimed there were racial undertones within Sydney’s comments.\nOn TikTok , one said, “A blonde haired, blue-eyed white woman is talking about her genes. Like, that is Nazi propaganda.”\nAnother added, “Hey American Eagle, now do black and brown women. Because black and brown women also have great genes that they inherit from their parents. Did you know that?”\nAmerican Eagle’s initial statement regarding their ad states, \"'Sydney Sweeney Has Great Jeans’ is and always was about the jeans. Her jeans. Her story. We’ll continue to celebrate how everyone wears their AE jeans with confidence, their way. Great jeans look good on everyone.”\nSydney Sweeney has not commented on the controversial ad.",
